      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel like a massive investment yielded nothing when you're facing this kind of sudden void. That feeling of being cheated by the system is a valid response to such a huge loss of perceived value. Instead of viewing it as a return of zero, perhaps you can see the accumulated knowledge as a foundation, even if it's a messy one. You don't have to \"reap rewards\" immediately; you can simply take a moment to acknowledge the sheer weight of what you've endured.",
      "source": "target",
